      "fv_empid_warn": "The Empidonax flycatchers overlap heavily, and silent birds often cannot be identified to species by sight at all — even experienced birders leave many as \"Empidonax sp.\" and call them on voice instead. Treat this drawing as showing the tendency, not a guarantee.",
      "fv_empid_warn_title": "⚠ Be careful with this one. ",
      "fv_plate_note": "This group sorts on what surrounds the eye: nothing at all, a bold complete ring, or spectacles — a ring joined to the bill by a short line. Then check the bill: flycatchers have a broad flat one, vireos a thicker one with a hooked tip.",
      "fv_plate_title": "Start at the eye, then the bill",
      "gamebird_walking": "Gamebird (walking)",
      "glossary_search_label": "Search birding glossary",
      "glossary_see_topography": "Body-part terms (lore, malar, nape, rump...) are drawn on a labelled bird in the Bird Topography Lab",
      "gull_breeding": "Adult breeding",
      "gull_first": "First winter",
      "gull_stage_note": "The brown streaky bird and the clean grey-and-white one on the same beach are often the same species at different ages. Large gulls pass through several intermediate plumages not drawn here, so a bird that matches none of these three is probably a middle year rather than a different species.",
      "gull_stage_title": "Same bird, {y} years apart — this is why gulls are hard",
      "gull_winter": "Adult winter",
      "irrupt_chart_alt": "Schematic chart. A regular winter visitor shows bars of similar height every winter. An irruptive visitor shows near-zero bars most winters and three very tall bars. A row below marks the northern seed crop as good or failed, and the failed crops line up with the tall bars.",
      "irrupt_chart_note": "A regular visitor turns up in similar numbers every winter. An irruptive one is absent, absent, absent — then floods south in one winter. The bottom row is why: when the northern seed or cone crop fails (✗), the birds have to leave. Schematic, to show the shape of the pattern — not counts for any one species.",
      "irrupt_chart_title": "What \"irruptive\" means — ten winters, same feeder",
