      "sa_alt": "Timeline from March to May. Each species is a bar spanning its arrival window, sorted earliest first. Blackbirds, robins and grackles arrive in March; loons and the first flycatchers in April; most warblers, thrushes and flycatchers cluster in mid May.",
      "sa_apr": "APR",
      "sa_mar": "MAR",
      "sa_may": "MAY",
      "sa_note": "Sorted by arrival, not alphabetically, so the wave is visible: a thin early trickle of blackbirds and robins, then a broad pile-up in mid May when most insect-eaters arrive at once. Bars show the window each species is expected in, not a single date — arrival shifts with the season and with the weather.",
