      "every_second_counts_for_emergency_resp": "Every second counts for emergency responders. A 1-minute delay reaching a cardiac arrest patient reduces survival by 10%. In Maine, failure to yield to an emergency vehicle is a Class E crime with at least a $250 fine for a first offense; repeat offenses can trigger license suspension.",
